      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "In CH3CN, 1 shows ligand-centered visible emission at 502 nm and Yb(III) NIR emission at 980 nm (2F5/2 → 2F7/2) under ligand excitation (λex = 416 nm). Lifetime 7.83 μs and Φem = 0.24%; estimated ΦLn = 0.4% and ηsens = 60%. NIR luminescence is enhanced by Na(I), Zn(II), Cd(II), Mg(II), and Pb(II), and quenched by Cr(III), Hg(II), Mn(II), Ni(II), Fe(III), Cu(II), Co(II), and nitro explosives, with highest sensitivity to Co(II), Cu(II), and picric acid (PA). Demonstrated NIR luminescent sensing of metal ions and nitro explosives at ppm level, including recyclable PA detection.",
